                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f1e042ad-f225-3969-bdd7-08d95e031c92",
                        "entry_id": "ec631dfb-3fe5-3950-b50b-aefcc4ef9a09",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A grasshopper."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "14e10233-9e93-4fd6-8625-2a2b01488b08",
                                "sense_id": "f1e042ad-f225-3969-bdd7-08d95e031c92",
                                "text": "But by the scorched bank-sides i' thy footsteps still I go plodding: Hedge-rows hot do resound with grasshops mournfully squeaking."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd90c11d-ffb1-4c85-a19e-3b70cd8a1e48",
                                "sense_id": "f1e042ad-f225-3969-bdd7-08d95e031c92",
                                "text": "I don't want grasshops tew giv [sic] entirely out, not if they are a blessing, but i hav thought (to myself) if they would let the grass and cornstalks be, and pitch onto the burdoks and Canada thissells, i would bet a few dollars on the thissells, jist tew encourage the fight, and wouldn't care a cuss if they both got finally licked."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d04fd26-ab0f-4bb6-8696-e192214124fc",
                                "sense_id": "f1e042ad-f225-3969-bdd7-08d95e031c92",
                                "text": "The margin was illumined all with golden rails And bees, enpictured with grasshops and wasps, With butterflies and fresh peacock tails, Engloried with flowers and slimy snails; [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "873659f6-ca09-42e2-a5ee-82e00a967af8",
                                "sense_id": "f1e042ad-f225-3969-bdd7-08d95e031c92",
                                "text": "[...] between a gulp and a vomit, when they're looking at you like you're the dumb one so you can't keep on staring at them. Maybe she ate grasshops. Maybe somebody put out food. I put out food."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
